course: dictionary
lesson: 7321
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Plain is a word with several meanings, so you cannot pick one until you read the words around it. Ask: what does the sentence need here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Water looks plain, but it is a very strange liquid.» Here plain means ordinary, with nothing fancy about how it looks. Swap in «ordinary» and the sentence still works.
explain: «It was plain that he was tired.» Here plain means easy to see or understand. Swap in «clear» and the meaning stays the same. The word plain changes meaning, but the clues in the sentence show you which one to use.
fact: Plain can be an adjective, a noun or an adverb.
fact: «Plain» as an adjective can mean simple, with nothing added, as in «plain yogurt».
fact: «Plain» can also mean easy to see or understand, as in «it was plain that he was tired».
fact: A plain is a large, flat area of land with few trees, like the Great Plains of North America.
fact: «Plain» as an adverb means completely, as in «plain silly».
exercise: Gritters spread salt because salty water freezes at a lower temperature than «plain water». What does plain water mean here? | Water that is very cold | Water that is easy to see through | Water that comes from a plain | *Water with nothing added
exercise: When New Horizons flew past Pluto, it found «a heart-shaped plain of nitrogen ice». What is a plain in this sentence? | *A large, flat area of land | A kind of puzzle | A thin blue haze | Cloud in the sky
exercise: Mum says, «That idea is plain silly.» What does plain mean here? | Flat | *Completely | Simple | Easy to see
test: «The answer was in plain sight on the board.» What does plain sight mean? | Very dark | Hidden under a cloth | Far away | *Easy to see
test: «It was plain that he was tired.» Which word could replace plain? | *Clear | Lovely | Ancient | Hungry
exam: In the puzzle, the instructions say «use the plain meanings for the next step». Which meaning fits best? | Very old | Dressed up in fancy clothes | A large, flat field | *Simple and clear, with nothing hidden
